{"Title":"An Act relative to Constitutional rights ","BillNumber":"H2391","DocketNumber":"HD2978","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"D_R1","Name":"David Allen Robertson","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/D_R1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-19T21:02:35.177"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"D_R1","Name":"David Allen Robertson","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/D_R1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-19T21:02:35.1766667"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H2391/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Robertson of Tewksbury, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 2391) of David Allen Robertson relative to protecting the rights of lawful gun owners.  Public Safety and Homeland Security.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. Chapter 140 shall be amended by inserting the following section:-\r\n\tSection 120A. No county, municipality, township or other community entity within the Commonwealth of Massachusetts may enact, pass or enforce any law, ordinance or regulation concerning the lawful ownership, use, possession, transfer, purchase, receipt or transportation of weapons, antique weapons, ammunition or ammunition components.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J22","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J22"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}